 "notes": "Libretto by Emanuel Schikaneder (1791). Words as printed in the Edition Peters vocal score, which the app follows where it differs from the libretto: \"Was soll das bedeuten?\" (the libretto has \"dies\"), \"gethan\" in the old spelling, \"wollt'\" and \"kröch'\" with the print's apostrophes, and Pamina's \"Die Wahrheit, die Wahrheit! wär' sie auch Verbrechen!\" (the libretto has \"Die Wahrheit – sei sie auch Verbrechen!\"). The chorus (sopranos, altos, tenors, basses: first offstage, then on stage greeting Sarastro) is heard with the piano and has no phrases here. IPA follows sung German stage diction: final -er, -ern as [ɐ]; the prefixes er-, ver-, zer- with [ɛr]; r elsewhere rolled or flipped; ch as [ç] after front vowels and [x] after back vowels; glottal stops [ʔ] before initial vowels; final b d g devoiced.",
